  "id": "work-ethic",
  "term": "work ethic",
  "definition": "Work ethic is a set of values and attitudes about work, in the classical Weberian sense, that treats work as central and important and emphasizes hard work, duty, self-reliance, avoiding wasted time, postponing immediate rewards, and a negative view of excessive leisure. In the source, these values are linked with both internally driven motivation to work and motivation tied to success, rewards, and social approval.",
